From 23651cf9ee8e143f6d211e0d7c47911c1f70c333 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: sixvolts <rigel@sixvolts.org>
Date: Sun, 4 Oct 2026 03:07:57 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] cuda: K-quant expert matvec thread-packed for short rows
 (P3), Q8_0 dense dispatch by K, Q8_0 hoist opt-in, MMQ scale rows

- mul_mat_vec_kq_repacked_pack<type, DOWN_R>: the Q5_1 pack kernel's mapping (thread -> (row,
  sub-block), 256/n_sub rows per group, DOWN_R groups per block, planes loaded before the first
  dot, LDS row sums) for Q4_K/Q5_K/Q6_K experts with K <= 2048 (crossport P3/R4: the Qwen 3.6-35B-A3B
  class down projection, K = 768). test-repack-bench 768x2048x128 (8 of 128 experts), per call:
  Q5_K 60.8 -> 34.6 us, Q6_K 63.4 -> 48.5, Q4_K 51.6 -> 44.3 (reinstinct's trace had the fork's
  Q5_K down at 38.1 vs its 13.4 us; 36 calls/token). GGML_CUDA_KQ_DOWN_R (default 4, 0 = the
  per-slot 2-row kernels).
- Dense Q8_0 at >= 512 rows: K = 4096 runs 2 rows per 64-thread block (4096x2048, the 35B's
  ssm_out/attn_output: one-wave loop 67 us, row-unrolled 53, two rows 29.7 = canonical; 4096x2816
  41 -> 34), K = 6144 keeps the row-unrolled kernel (43.7 vs 46.7 two-row). GGML_CUDA_Q8_ROWU
  = all | r2 | old selects the mapping for A/B.
- The generic Q8_0 matvec hoist is opt-in (GGML_CUDA_Q8_HOIST=1): reinstinct's in-model A/B on
  Gemma 26B-A4B (graphs on, tg128) measured 97 -> 90.5 tok/s with it although every shape is level
  standalone, and no model measured here gains from it.
- MMQ scale rows: float2 rows (K-quant, Q5_1, Q8_0 tiles) stay padded to [BK+1] (b64 loads keep
  their alignment; the Q5_1 MoE tile measured 4.54 vs 4.23 TMAC/s with them padded), the nibble
  tile's float rows are unpadded again: with a 20 B stride the compiler split the four kk scales'
  b128 load into b32 pairs (reinstinct's ISA diff of the shipped tile vs the harness: 32 vs 36
  ds_read_b128), which held the Q4_0 tile at 9.9 TMAC/s; now 11.27, equal to reinstinct's tile.
- test-repack-bench: 35B-class MoE down shapes (Q4_K/Q5_K/Q6_K 768x2048x128) and the 26B/35B dense
  Q8_0 shapes.

Flash-Next (4x MI50): pp512 781, pp2048 1325, tg64 52.8-52.9 (deployed ae7fdb2d7: 788 / 1335 / 52.0,
within run noise). --check passes with every switch setting.

